{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/2021-01-15---Visualizing-The-Language-Migration-Of-A-Codebase/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"eb6c6500-90e3-5b36-8b47-a48124149e52","html":"<p>If you’ve ever gone through the trouble of incrementally migrating a codebase from one language to another then you know this is not something that gets done in a few weeks. You can mark all the milestones you want but in the end nothing beats a nice graph that shows continuous improvements to your stakeholders.</p>\n<p>Github has this very useful feature where it shows the language distribution of your repo at that point in time. What we want is this, but then for each day — and ideally, we won’t be taking notes manually every time.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/be988dba76414fb6522393628dd108ac/github.png\" alt=\"Repo language distribution on Github\"></p>\n<p>So I’ve done exactly that with the following bash script:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"bash\"><pre class=\"language-bash\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"token shebang important\">#!/usr/local/bin/bash</span>\r\n<span class=\"token assign-left variable\">repo</span><span class=\"token operator\">=~</span>/Documents/source/my-repo\r\n<span class=\"token assign-left variable\">branch</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"master\"</span>\r\n<span class=\"token assign-left variable\">startdate</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token number\">2019</span>-05-01\r\n<span class=\"token assign-left variable\">enddate</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token number\">2021</span>-01-15\r\n<span class=\"token builtin class-name\">declare</span> <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-A</span> <span class=\"token assign-left variable\">langs</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">\"JavaScript\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token number\">0</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">\"TypeScript\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\r\n\r\n<span class=\"token keyword\">for</span> <span class=\"token for-or-select variable\">key</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token operator\">!</span>langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>@<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">do</span> <span class=\"token assign-left variable\">pattern</span><span class=\"token operator\">+=</span><span class=\"token string\">'%-15s,'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">done</span>\r\n<span class=\"token builtin class-name\">cd</span> <span class=\"token variable\">$repo</span>\r\n<span class=\"token assign-left variable\">regex</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"([0-9]+\\.[0-9]+)%[[:space:]]*([A-Za-z#-]*)\"</span>\r\n<span class=\"token builtin class-name\">printf</span> <span class=\"token string\">'%-15s, %s'</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"Date\"</span>\r\n<span class=\"token builtin class-name\">printf</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$pattern</span> %s<span class=\"token entity\" title=\"\\n\">\\n</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token operator\">!</span>langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>@<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span>\r\n\r\n<span class=\"token keyword\">while</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$startdate</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token operator\">!=</span> <span class=\"token variable\">$enddate</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">do</span>\r\n    <span class=\"token function\">git</span> checkout <span class=\"token variable\"><span class=\"token variable\">`</span><span class=\"token function\">git</span> rev-list <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-1</span> <span class=\"token parameter variable\">--before</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$startdate</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$branch</span>\"</span><span class=\"token variable\">`</span></span> <span class=\"token operator\">></span> /dev/null <span class=\"token operator\"><span class=\"token file-descriptor important\">2</span>></span><span class=\"token file-descriptor important\">&amp;1</span>\r\n    <span class=\"token assign-left variable\">table</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\"><span class=\"token variable\">$(</span>github-linguist<span class=\"token variable\">)</span></span>\"</span>\r\n    <span class=\"token builtin class-name\">printf</span> <span class=\"token string\">'%-15s, %s'</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$startdate</span>\"</span>\r\n\r\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">while</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span> <span class=\"token variable\">$table</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=~</span> <span class=\"token variable\">$regex</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">do</span>\r\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">for</span> <span class=\"token for-or-select variable\">lang</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token operator\">!</span>langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>@<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span>\r\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">do</span>\r\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$lang</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token operator\">==</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token environment constant\">BASH_REMATCH</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>2<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">then</span>\r\n                langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token variable\">$lang</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token environment constant\">BASH_REMATCH</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>1<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span>\r\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">fi</span>\r\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">done</span>\r\n        <span class=\"token assign-left variable\">table</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token variable\">${table<span class=\"token operator\">##</span>*${<span class=\"token environment constant\">BASH_REMATCH</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>1<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\r\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">done</span>\r\n\r\n    <span class=\"token builtin class-name\">printf</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">$pattern</span> %s<span class=\"token entity\" title=\"\\n\">\\n</span>\"</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>@<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span>\r\n    <span class=\"token assign-left variable\">startdate</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token variable\"><span class=\"token variable\">$(</span><span class=\"token function\">date</span> <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-j</span> <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-v</span> +1d <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-f</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"%Y-%m-%d\"</span> $startdate +%Y-%m-%d<span class=\"token variable\">)</span></span>\r\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">for</span> <span class=\"token for-or-select variable\">key</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"<span class=\"token variable\">${<span class=\"token operator\">!</span>langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>@<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>}</span>\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">do</span> langs<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token variable\">$key</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token number\">0</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">done</span>\r\n<span class=\"token keyword\">done</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>First, some prerequisites:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Follow the install instructions for github-linguist <a href=\"https://github.com/github/linguist\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">here</a>. If you use a recent MacOS version like me then you’re likely to bump into some issues getting it running. I’ve documented them <a href=\"https://github.com/github/linguist/issues/5147#issuecomment-761017609\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">here</a>. The latest version of github-linguist is incompatible so you’ll need a specific version like <a href=\"https://github.com/github/linguist/packages/18032?version=7.11.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">7.11</a>. Later versions change the console output which is incompatible with this script.</li>\n<li>I ran <code class=\"language-text\">sudo gem pristine curb --version 0.9.10</code> to remove some unwanted console output</li>\n<li>You’ll need Bash 4 to support hash tables so run <code class=\"language-text\">brew install bash</code> to get the latest version</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Some tricky aspects worth calling out:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bash regex is a different dialect than most people I’d wager are used to. <code class=\"language-text\">\\d</code> does not exist and needs to be replaced with <code class=\"language-text\">[0-9]</code> instead. Similarly, <code class=\"language-text\">[[:space:]]</code> is roughly equivalent to <code class=\"language-text\">\\s</code>.</li>\n<li>While we’re talking about regex, iterating through the regex matches is an absolute pain. I still don’t fully understand what <code class=\"language-text\">table=${table##*${BASH_REMATCH[1]}}</code> does but it works so I’m not touching it (credit to <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/PandaEox/5215e33dca9c14076eff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">this gist</a>).</li>\n<li>To get the values from a hash table, you use <code class=\"language-text\">${langs[@]}</code>. To get the keys, you use <code class=\"language-text\">${!langs[@]}</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The overarching idea behind this is straightforward:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check out the code at a given date</li>\n<li>Run github-linguist to determine the language distribution</li>\n<li>Parse the output and re-output it in a format that is better for us</li>\n<li>Go to the next day and return to step 2</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This will give you an output like this:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"text\"><pre class=\"language-text\"><code class=\"language-text\">Date           , TypeScript     ,JavaScript     ,Objective-C    ,Swift          , \r\n2020-08-13     , 20.25          ,48.42          ,4.32           ,12.76          , \r\n2020-08-14     , 20.19          ,48.29          ,4.30           ,13.00          , \r\n2020-08-15     , 20.19          ,48.29          ,4.30           ,13.00          , \r\n2020-08-16     , 20.19          ,48.29          ,4.30           ,13.00          , \r\n2020-08-17     , 20.26          ,48.43          ,4.32           ,13.28          , \r\n2020-08-18     , 20.26          ,48.43          ,4.32           ,13.28          , \r\n2020-08-19     , 20.22          ,48.35          ,4.31           ,13.45          , \r\n2020-08-20     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-21     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-22     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-23     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-24     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-25     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-26     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-27     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-28     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-29     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , \r\n2020-08-30     , 26.59          ,41.29          ,4.38           ,13.87          , </code></pre></div>\n<p>The commas make it look a little bit off but they exist for a reason: now we use the power of <a href=\"https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9308645?hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Google Sheets</a>. Using this format, we can simply copy-paste our console output into a sheet.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 770px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/f4b77/pasting.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 156.25%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/8ac56/pasting.webp 240w,\n/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/d3be9/pasting.webp 480w,\n/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/cf403/pasting.webp 770w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 770px) 100vw, 770px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/8ff5a/pasting.png 240w,\n/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/e85cb/pasting.png 480w,\n/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/f4b77/pasting.png 770w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 770px) 100vw, 770px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/2e80213aabfefa85da29a6f353003dcb/f4b77/pasting.png\"\n            alt=\"Pasting the raw data into Google Sheets\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>When doing so, Google Sheets will suggest to split it into columns and produce a nicely separated table:</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/45662/splitting.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 65.83333333333333%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/8ac56/splitting.webp 240w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/d3be9/splitting.webp 480w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/e46b2/splitting.webp 960w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/e97dc/splitting.webp 1410w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/8ff5a/splitting.png 240w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/e85cb/splitting.png 480w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/d9199/splitting.png 960w,\n/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/45662/splitting.png 1410w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/66acafd3166b957ad38b065070b7d139/d9199/splitting.png\"\n            alt=\"Splitting the columns using the separator\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Creating a chart is now trivial and gives you something like this:</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/8cdda/viewing.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 60.416666666666664%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/8ac56/viewing.webp 240w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/d3be9/viewing.webp 480w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/e46b2/viewing.webp 960w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/2768a/viewing.webp 1168w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/8ff5a/viewing.png 240w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/e85cb/viewing.png 480w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/d9199/viewing.png 960w,\n/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/8cdda/viewing.png 1168w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/8c6944a7d8cdd9aa5ac17f120fef8e2a/d9199/viewing.png\"\n            alt=\"The eventual chart\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Of course this is only looking at a very short period of time. The longer the timespan, the more useful your charts will be, e.g.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/02dd8e07e8613c9da0eafd11e6755284/bigchart.png\" alt=\"The eventual chart\"></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>⚠️ NOTE:</strong>  Getting an error like <code class=\"language-text\">dlopen(/Library/Ruby/Gems/2.3.0/gems/charlock_holmes-0.7.6/lib/charlock_holmes/charlock_holmes.bundle, 0x0009): dependent dylib '/usr/local/opt/icu4c/lib/libicudata.64.dylib' not found for '/Library/Ruby/Gems/2.3.0/gems/charlock_holmes-0.7.6/lib/charlock_holmes/charlock_holmes.bundle' - /Library/Ruby/Gems/2.3.0/gems/charlock_holmes-0.7.6/lib/charlock_holmes/charlock_holmes.bundle (LoadError)</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Reinstall charlock_holmes, you’ve probably <a href=\"https://github.com/github/linguist/issues/4879#issuecomment-640455585\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">updated a dependency</a>! I’ve reinstalled it using <code class=\"language-text\">sudo gem install charlock_holmes -- --with-icu-dir=/usr/local/opt/icu4c --with-cxxflags='-Wno-reserved-user-defined-literal -std=c++11'</code></p>","fields":{"slug":"/posts/2021-01-15---Visualizing-The-Language-Migration-Of-A-Codebase/","tagSlugs":["/tag/javascript/","/tag/typescript/","/tag/bash/","/tag/shell/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2021-01-16T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["Javascript","Typescript","Bash","Shell"],"title":"Visualizing the language migration of a codebase","description":"Migrating a codebase from one language to another is a long journey. Using a simple shell script you can create a quick and useful visual.","socialImage":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2021-01-15---Visualizing-The-Language-Migration-Of-A-Codebase/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}